# `railway up` uploads the working directory as the build context. It already
# honours .gitignore, but `.env` is worth excluding explicitly and belt-and-
# braces: every entrypoint calls `loadEnvFile()` (src/adapters/load-env.ts),
# so a `.env` that reached the image would *override* the variables Railway
# injects — pointing a deployed service at `localhost:5432` and leaking real
# Razorpay keys into the build context at the same time. Neither failure is
# loud; both are avoided here rather than relied on not to happen.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
web/node_modules
dist
web/dist

# Local-only scratch: never part of a deployed image.
.tmp-probe
*.log
